hile a source tab is on screen the palette lists those chords' actions as items of kind Editor, under Monaco's own labels with the old chord as the hint, and runs the chosen one on the tab through the editor status store's `action` ask. Pin Editor and Unpin Editor are Editor items too, listed with Cmd+K Shift+Enter, VS Code's chord, whenever the pane that last held the focus has a tab; each acts on that pane's active tab (`pinItems` of `state/workbench/palette.ts`). A palette row is one line: a title longer than the row is cut with an ellipsis (`shell/keys/PaletteRow.svelte`) and the whole title is the row's tooltip. The palette lists three more Editor items while the tab's text holds a quick diff mark: Go to Next Change on Alt+F5 and Go to Previous Change on Shift+Alt+F5, VS Code's keys, which put the caret on the next or previous mark and go round at the ends, and Open Change, which opens the diff at the mark on the caret's line; like VS Code, a file with no mark offers none of the three. The editor keeps Monaco's own right-click menu, VS Code's editor menu, in the tokens' colours. A source tab over a file of a repository draws VS Code's quick diff in its gutter, from the marks and blame words of `state/sources/repositories/file-git.ts`: in the editor as Monaco line decorations in the lane beside the line numbers (`ui/controls/editor/gutter/gutter.ts`), and in the read-only code window through `views/sources/source/Gutter.svelte`. An added run, a modified run and the place a deletion took lines out, each against the index and read again on a save and whenever the repository's state moves, and a press on a mark opens the file's diff at that change. The Toggle Blame button of the breadcrumb bar and the palette's Git: Toggle Git Blame Editor Decoration, kept with the draft, add who last changed each line of the saved file and when to the line-number column, on the first line of each run from one commit (in the editor through Monaco's `lineNumbers` function, the column widened to hold it), with the commit and its subject on hover and Not Committed Yet for a line no commit holds, and a press on a blamed line opens its commit in the Repositories view's graph. The blame is read whenever the file is in a repository and its text was read, since the status bar says the caret line's blame whether or not the column draws it; a file a read refused asks for no blame. A tab over the file at HEAD or in the index reads the blame of that version through `GET /api/git?blame=<root>&path=<path>&stage=head|index` (any other `stage` is answered 400) and no marks, and offers Toggle Blame as its one action.
